  "title": "Chapter 39: National Parks and Wildlife Sanctuaries of India",
  "order": 39,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tlwdsb5",
      "content": "India is one of the world's richest countries in terms of biodiversity. To conserve wildlife and their habitats, the Government of India has created protected areas such as National Parks, Wildlife Sanctuaries, Biosphere Reserves, Tiger Reserves and Bird Sanctuaries."
    },
