      "id": "c20fen1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Types of Protected Areas in India"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "India's network of protected areas includes National Parks, Wildlife Sanctuaries, Conservation Reserves, and Biosphere Reserves.",
        "Jim Corbett National Park (established in 1936 as Hailey National Park) is the oldest national park in India.",
        "Hemis National Park in Ladakh is the largest national park in India by area.",
        "Project Tiger was initiated in 1973 to save the Bengal tiger from extinction, leading to the creation of designated Tiger Reserves."
      ],
      "id": "mhrh7ia"
    },
