    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Crucial distinction: Grazing and human settlements are completely prohibited in National Parks, whereas limited human activities are allowed in Wildlife Sanctuaries.",
        "Wildlife Protection Act of 1972 provides the legal framework for establishing protected areas in India.",
        "Major species-specific conservation programs: Project Tiger (1973), Project Elephant (1992), and Project Snow Leopard (2009)."
      ],
